\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Structured output.
\f0\b0  Every topic gets discussed twice: once at the model level (
\f2\fs26 with_structured_output
\f0\fs24 ) and once at the agent level (
\f2\fs26 response_format
\f0\fs24 ). Both bottom out in the model. 
\f2\fs26 ToolStrategy
\f0\fs24  is a LangChain feature, not a model feature \'97 the tool it uses internally sits on the LangChain side, because a model can never call a tool.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 15-tickets debate, settled.
\f0\b0  Whether an over-limit request should be split into 10 + 5 is a product decision, not a developer one. If someone asks for 900 you won't book ninety batches of ten. The developer's job is that the ceiling holds without fail.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Don't prompt your way out of a code problem.
\f0\b0  The instinct to add "please don't make mistakes, you're a very smart model" to the system prompt is the wrong reflex. Enforce it in code where you can.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pre-built tools are just functions.
\f0\b0  
\f2\fs26 langchain-tavily
\f0\fs24  gives you a function you didn't have to write. Nothing more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
