\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. Agents\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 The agentic loop\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 An agent is a 
\f2\fs26 while
\f0\fs24  loop: receive message 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  request tool call 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  execute tool 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  append result 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  repeat until done. The model reports a stop reason when it's finished or wants to ask something.\
He prefers 
\f1\b "agentic loop"
\f0\b0  to "ReAct pattern" as terminology now.\
Guard against infinite loops with a max-turns condition, as in the earlier plain-Python build.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Agent = model + harness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A reflection worth recording: in the last four or five years, the only genuinely new thing is the artificial brain. Everything around it \'97 tools, messages, memory, orchestration \'97 is ordinary software engineering. The work is harnessing the model well.\
By now the components have all been covered: models, messages, tools, structured output. Still to come: memory, sub-agents, skills, middleware.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

