\f2\fs26 \cf0 @tool\
def get_real_weather(city: str) -> str:\
    """Get the current weather for a city."""\
    geo = requests.get("https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search", params=\{"name": city\}).json()\
    ...\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Verified against Tokyo, New Delhi and Bengaluru with plausible readings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 2. Tavily search
\f0\b0  \'97 third-party service; LangChain provides the integration, the key and quota are yours.\

\f1\b 3 & 4. 
\f4\fs26 save_trip
\f1\fs24  / 
\f4\fs26 get_saved_trips
\f0\b0\fs24  \'97 backed by SQLite:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 def setup_database():\
    conn = sqlite3.connect("tripmate.db")\
    conn.execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS trips (...)")\
    conn.commit()\
    conn.close()\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 On the repeated "why SQLite and not Chroma/Postgres/Mongo?" question: it doesn't matter. It's a database. SQLite is the easiest thing to mock up locally. Whichever one you name, someone will ask why not the other.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
