\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 8. Q&A worth keeping\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 When to use what \'97 store vs checkpointer vs cache vs database.
\f0\b0  No universal answer; it depends on the application.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f5\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Chat history
\f0\i0 : keep in memory if the session is disposable (Swiggy/Amazon support chats that expire), persist if you need it across days like ChatGPT. Storage on a fast-retrieval DB is expensive at scale.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f5\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Store
\f0\i0 : things needed across sessions \'97 "I prefer Python examples" \'97 i.e. long-term memory.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f5\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Database
\f0\i0 : the source of truth for the whole application. Predates AI, unchanged by it. Users can edit their stored preferences; they can't rewrite your logs.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f5\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Caching
\f0\i0 : a million identical "weather in Delhi" requests don't each need an API call. Cache the response for an hour or a day.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f5\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prompt caching
\f0\i0 : a different thing entirely \'97 the provider caches the earlier turns so you send only the new message. Claude caches for roughly an hour.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Tool failures.
\f0\b0  Retries depend on the failure type and the harness you build. Fatal errors surface as errors, the same way ChatGPT fails when your connection drops.\

\f1\b Runtime tool discovery.
\f0\b0  Yes, via MCP \'97 again through middleware.\

\f1\b Performance for a single user.
\f0\b0  Not a scaling question. Find where the time actually goes: LangSmith for the agent layer, logs for everything else. No single tool answers it.\

\f1\b Interview technique.
\f0\b0  When asked "what's the best X?", ask follow-ups back \'97 what are you optimising for, under what constraints. There's rarely one right answer, and saying so with the right questions is the answer.\

\f1\b An earlier version of this course
\f0\b0  covered the older LangChain. Stick with 1.0; the previous version will eventually be decommissioned.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
